 "_notes": " 2026-08-28: four uncontested races added from the Town Clerk's \"Results of elections\" sheet (records-request reply). The Berkshire Eagle independently names the same four winners -- \"Mark Phelps was elected to the Select Board, Kurt Singer to the Board of Health, and Diane George and Tammy Steinhoff to the Planning Board\" -- so the names are corroborated and the sheet supplies the counts. BALLOT COUNT CONFLICT, RESOLVED AGAINST THE SHEET: the sheet says 51 ballots cast; the Eagle, quoting the same clerk the day after, says \"With 57 of the town's 194 registered voters casting ballots, turnout was 29 percent\". 45 + 12 in the contested School Committee race is 57, and 57/194 = 29.4% while 51/194 = 26.3%. Three facts cohere on 57 and only the sheet says 51, so 57 stands and the discrepancy is recorded rather than smoothed away.",
